📈 CodeAlpha Stock Portfolio Tracker

A simple Stock Portfolio Tracker developed using Python as part of the CodeAlpha Python Programming Internship.

The program allows users to enter stock names and quantities, calculates the value of each investment using predefined stock prices, and displays the total portfolio investment value.

📌 Project Overview

The Stock Portfolio Tracker is a console-based Python application designed to demonstrate basic programming and file-handling concepts.

The program uses a predefined dictionary containing stock symbols and their prices. Users can select stocks and enter the quantity they own. The program then calculates the total investment value.

🎯 Objective

The main objective of this project is to practice Python programming concepts by building a simple portfolio tracking application.

The project allows the user to:

Select stocks from a predefined list.
Enter the quantity of stocks.
Calculate individual investment values.
Calculate the total portfolio value.
Save the portfolio summary to a text file.
✨ Features
📊 Predefined stock price dictionary
📈 Multiple stock selection
🔢 Quantity-based investment calculation
💰 Total investment calculation
✅ Stock validation
📄 Portfolio summary saved to .txt
💻 Simple console-based interface

